
  <sn><md>## Creating an Rclone Google Drive Remote {.text-center}

For a normal Ubuntu/Linux desktop with a browser, the complete process is:

The exact questions can vary slightly depending on your **Rclone version and Google Drive backend**, so don't worry if your prompts aren't word-for-word identical. The important decisions for a normal personal Google Drive are generally:

| Setting            | Choice       |
| ------------------ | ------------ |
| Remote name        | `gdrive`     |
| Storage            | Google Drive |
| Client ID          | Empty        |
| Client secret      | Empty        |
| Scope              | `1`          |
| Root folder ID     | Empty        |
| Service account    | Empty        |
| Advanced config    | `n`          |
| Auto config        | `y`          |
| Shared Drive       | `n`          |
| Save configuration | `y`          |

[Rclone Google Drive documentation](https://rclone.org/drive/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)


</md></sn>
  <sn><md>### Start Rclone configuration

```bash
rclone config
```

Choose:

```text
n) New remote
```

Enter:

```text
n
```</md></sn><config>
