<sn><md>### Enter a remote name

Rclone asks:

```text
name&gt;
```

For example:

```text
name&gt; gdrive
```

Your remote will then be called:

```text
gdrive:
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Select Google Drive

Rclone displays a list of storage providers with numbers.

Find:

```text
Google Drive
```

and enter its corresponding number.

**Don't use a fixed number from an example**, because the provider list can change between Rclone versions.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Configure Google OAuth credentials

You may see:

```text
client_id&gt;
```

Press **Enter** to use Rclone's default client.

Then:

```text
client_secret&gt;
```

Press **Enter** again.

For a normal personal Google Drive setup, you generally don't need to create your own Google API credentials.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Select the access scope

Rclone asks:

```text
scope&gt;
```

For normal full synchronization/backup, choose:

```text
1
```

This gives Rclone full access to the Drive files needed for normal operations.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Root folder ID

You may see:

```text
root_folder_id&gt;
```

Press **Enter**.

This makes Rclone use the normal Google Drive root.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Service account

You may see:

```text
service_account_file&gt;
```

Press **Enter**.

You don't need a service account for a normal personal Google account.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Advanced configuration

Rclone may ask:

```text
Edit advanced config?
y) Yes
n) No
```

Choose:

```text
n
```

For a basic setup.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Browser authentication

You should then see something like:

```text
Use auto config?
y) Yes
n) No
```

Because you're using a Linux desktop with a browser, choose:

```text
y
```

Rclone will open your browser.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Google authentication

In the browser:

```text
Google account
      ↓
Sign in
      ↓
Grant Rclone permission
      ↓
Authentication completed
```

Return to the terminal after authentication.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Shared Drive question

Rclone may ask:

```text
Configure this as a Shared Drive?
y) Yes
n) No
```

For your normal personal **My Drive**, choose:

```text
n
```

If you specifically want to connect a Google Workspace Shared Drive, choose `y`.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Confirm the remote

Rclone will show the configuration and ask something similar to:

```text
y) Yes this is OK
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
```

Choose:

```text
y
```

Then quit:

```text
q
```

</md></sn><sn><md>### Verify the remote

First:

```bash
rclone listremotes
```

You should see:

```text
gdrive:
```

Then list directories:

```bash
rclone lsd gdrive:
```

You can also list files:

```bash
rclone ls gdrive:
```

Or a more readable listing:

```bash
rclone lsf gdrive:
```

If these commands show your Google Drive contents, your remote is working.

</md></sn><sn></sn>